7, "id": "30", "resolution": "168x94"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OMjZeFobpU0/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEiCMQBEG5IWvKriqkDFQgBFQAAAAAYASUAAMhCPQCAokN4AQ==&rs=AOn4CLBsKvHnz4q0JJsDJ0bmNAbCg1KvkQ", "height": 110, "width": 196, "preference": -7, "id": "31", "resolution": "196x110"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OMjZeFobpU0/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEjCPYBEIoBSFryq4qpAxUIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAE=&rs=AOn4CLB8geLA9dyNMmqi7QCSImMLiAPFeg", "height": 138, "width": 246, "preference": -7, "id": "32", "resolution": "246x138"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OMjZeFobpU0/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEjCNACELwBSFryq4qpAxUIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAE=&rs=AOn4CLD7lFrtLaDetWGlb5M04u7G7caVQg", "height": 188, "width": 336, "preference": -7, "id": "33", "resolution": "336x188"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OMjZeFobpU0/hqdefault.jpg", "height": 360, "width": 480, "preference": -7, "id": "34", "resolution": "480x360"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/OMjZeFobpU0/hqdefault.webp", "preference": -6, "id": "35"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OMjZeFobpU0/sddefault.jpg", "height": 480, "width": 640, "preference": -5, "id": "36", "resolution": "640x480"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/OMjZeFobpU0/sddefault.webp", "preference": -4, "id": "37"}], "thumbnail": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OMjZeFobpU0/sddefault.jpg", "description": "Tanguar haor, located in the Dharmapasha and Tahirpur upazilas of Sunamganj District in Bangladesh. Tanguar haor is a unique wetland ecosystem of national importance and has come into international focus. \nThe total area of Tanguar haor including 46 villages within the haor is about 100km2. It is the source of livelihood for more than 40,000 people. \nIn 1999 The Government of Bangladesh declared Tanguar haor as an Ecologically Critical area  considering its critical condition as a result of over exploitation of its natural resources. \nThe hoar basin was declared a Ramsar site - wetland of international importance in 2000. After the  declaration, the Government is committed to preserve its natural resources and has taken several steps for protection of this wetland.\n\nTanguar haor plays an important role in fish production as it functions as a 'mother fishery' for the country.\n\nEvery winter the haor is home to about 200 types of migratory birds. The haor is an important source of fish. There are more than 140 species of fresh water fish in the haor. The more predominant among them are: ayir, gang magur, baim, tara, gutum, gulsha, tengra, titna, garia, beti, kakia etc. Hijal, karach, gulli, balua, ban tulsi, nalkhagra and other freshwater wetland trees are in this haor.\n\nPlant species like Hizol (Barringtonia acutangula), Clematis cadmia, Crataeva nurvala, Euryale ferox, Nelumbo nucifera, Ottelia alismoides, Oxystelma secamone var. secamone, Pongamia pinnata, Rosa clinophylla, and Typha species are present.", "channel_id": "UCYy-9m1lDNWauVp1EN8kf0g", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCYy-9m1lDNWauVp1EN8kf0g", "duration": 62, "view_count": 91, "age_limit": 0, "webpage_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OMjZeFobpU0", "categories": ["Travel & Events"], "tags": ["tanguar haor", "tanguar hawor", "travell", "bangladesh", "sunamganj", "travelers of bangladesh", "world tour", "tour", "world heritage", "world travell"], "playable_in_embed": true, "live_status": "not_live", "media_type": "video", "_format_sort_fields": ["quality", "res", "fps", "hdr:12", "source", "vcodec", "channels", "acodec", "lang", "proto"], "automatic_captions": {}, "subtitles": {}, "like_count": 2, "channel": "Scribble Workshop- HiZiBiZi", "channel_follower_count": 223, "uploader": "Scribble Workshop- HiZiBiZi", "uploader_id": "@GolmeleBlogspot", "uploader_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@GolmeleBlogspot", "upload_date": "20170808", "timestamp": 1502218852, "availability": "public", "webpage_url_basename": "watch", "webpage_url_domain": "youtube.com", "extractor": "youtube", "extractor_key": "Youtube", "display_id": "OMjZeFobpU